The roof of a tower is a right square pyramid with base edge $6\text{ m}$ and perpendicular height $10\text{ m}$.
Find the slant height $l$ of a sloping face in exact surd form.

development.solution_text:
Half the base edge is $6\div2=3\text{ m}$; this and the perpendicular height are the two shorter sides.
$l=\sqrt{10^{2}+3^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{109}\text{ m}$
