A right square pyramid has base edge $18\text{ cm}$ and slant height $15\text{ cm}$.
Find the perpendicular height $h$.

development.solution_text:
The slant height is the hypotenuse; half the base edge is $18\div2=9\text{ cm}$.
$h=\sqrt{15^{2}-9^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{144}$
$=12\text{ cm}$
